## What this is

__PROJECT_DESCRIPTION__

Each sub-repo is a self-contained git repo in a subfolder. The hub itself is a small git repo that tracks only this `CLAUDE.md`, `project.yaml`, `invoke-ai.sh`, `README.md`, and `.gitignore`. The sub-repo directories are listed in the managed block of `.gitignore` so they don't pollute the hub's git history.

## How Claude loads context

`./invoke-ai.sh` launches Claude with `--add-dir` for every sub-repo present locally. Claude Code automatically reads:

- This file (`<hub>/CLAUDE.md`) — high-level project map
- Each `<sub-repo>/CLAUDE.md` — rules specific to that codebase

Per-repo rules live in the repo they apply to. Edit `acme-app/CLAUDE.md` for app-specific conventions, etc.

