## Working with this hub

- `./invoke-ai.sh` — launch Claude with all accessible sub-repos mounted
- `/hub-clone-all` — clone every registered repo URL into a missing subfolder
- `/hub-sync` — `git pull` across all sub-repos
- `/hub-status` — aggregated git status across all sub-repos
- `/hub-scan` — detect un-registered sub-repos
- `/hub-add-repo` — register a new sub-repo (clone or adopt)
- `/hub-describe` — refresh sub-repo descriptions from their READMEs

## Access notes

Sub-repos you don't have git access to will simply be missing from disk and `invoke-ai.sh` will skip them with a warning. The hub itself contains no sensitive code — it's a meta repo, safe to share broadly.

Hub conventions are documented in `.claude/skills/project-hub-conventions/SKILL.md` (vendored locally — works without the ws-marketplace plugin installed).
